{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SITE HEADER — tablet and desktop · REFERENCE §7.1 · design/SiteHeader.dc.html
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  A 64px bar: the logo, TWO panel triggers (Participate, Explore), a toolbar pill
  (Search | Aa | language) and the account control. Hidden below 600px, where the phone
  has the app bar and the tab bar (chrome.css). Mounted by `layout/shell.twig`, never by
  a page, and it mounts no phone sheet (SiteHeaderTest).

  ── NO GREEN BUTTON, IN EITHER SIGNED-IN STATE ──────────────────────────────

  §6.1: green is THE primary action inside the page. A green pill in the chrome sits
  beside every page's own call to action and wins. Signed out is an outlined ink pill;
  signed in is the ink avatar.

  ── THE TWO LISTS ARE THE HANDOFF'S, EXACTLY ───────────────────────────────

  §7.1's six and six — and Explore is Discover, Pulse, Events, Legacy Vault, Blog,
  Status. The previous header carried a seventh, Results; the owner removed it on
  3 Oct 2026, and the guards that held it there were rewritten to the new rule. The DC
  draws Leaderboard and Shop where the phase file says Blog and Status; the phase file
  outranks the DC (REFERENCE §0). Status is not in the DC's list, so its line is the
  status page's own words from the DC's search data ("Is everything working?").

  Every tile's colour is a pair of Accent tokens named by a TONE class (chrome.css),
  never one of the DC's hexes: `#eef7ee`, `#a47306`, `#e9efef`, `#2b373d`, `#f0f2f2` and
  `#5d7374` are not in the palette, and a colour is typed in one file (CLAUDE.md).

  And a comment cannot go INSIDE the array below — Twig lexes a comment only between
  tags, and answers a stray hash in an array literal with a SyntaxError.

  ── THE CONTROLLER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  `public/assets/js/header.js`, binding the `data-ag-mega*` and `data-ag-pop*` hooks:
  click toggles, opening one closes every other panel and popover, Esc and the scrim
  close, focus returns to the trigger, arrow keys move inside a panel and along the
  toolbar (a `role="toolbar"` that only answers Tab is a toolbar in name).

  Search is an ANCHOR to Discover that the script upgrades to open the palette, so with
  scripting off it still goes somewhere a search can happen.
#}
{% set _ini = member_name ? (member_name|split(' ')|filter(w => w != '')|map(w => w|first)|join|upper|slice(0, 2)) : 'AG' %}
{% set _megas = [
  {k:'participate', label:'Participate', items:[
    {href:'/nominate',         label:'Nominate',           sub:'Put someone forward in under 90 seconds', tone:'grow',   d:'M12 5v14M5 12h14'},
    {href:'/vote',             label:'Vote',               sub:'One verified voter, one vote per category', tone:'act',  d:'M4 12.5 9 17.5 20 6.5'},
    {href:'/awards',           label:'Awards',             sub:'Every award, edition and category',       tone:'honour', d:'M5 16 3 6l5 4 4-6 4 6 5-4-2 10z'},
    {href:'/giving',           label:'Giving',             sub:'Back the programmes behind the awards',   tone:'give',   d:'M20.8 4.6a5.5 5.5 0 0 0-7.8 0L12 5.6l-1-1a5.5 5.5 0 0 0-7.8 7.8L12 21l8.8-8.6a5.5 5.5 0 0 0 0-7.8Z'},
    {href:'/account/register', label:'Register a profile', sub:'Join the continental registry, free',     tone:'honour', d:'M16 11a4 4 0 1 0-8 0M3 21a9 9 0 0 1 18 0'},
    {href:'/integrity',        label:'Integrity Center',   sub:'How voting, judging and audits work',     tone:'plain',  d:'M12 2.4l7.6 2.7v5.8c0 4.7-3.1 8.3-7.6 10-4.5-1.7-7.6-5.3-7.6-10V5.1z'}
  ]},
  {k:'explore', label:'Explore', items:[
    {href:'/discover', label:'Discover',     sub:'People, organisations and awards',     tone:'plain',  d:'M11 4a7 7 0 1 0 0 14 7 7 0 0 0 0-14ZM20 20l-3.6-3.6'},
    {href:'/pulse',    label:'Pulse',        sub:'Posts and live moments',               tone:'give',   d:'M5 3h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2ZM10 8.5l5 3.5-5 3.5z'},
    {href:'/events',   label:'Events',       sub:'Ceremonies, livestreams and sessions', tone:'act',    d:'M4 5h16v15H4zM4 10h16M9 3v4M15 3v4'},
    {href:'/legacy',   label:'Legacy Vault', sub:'Every edition, permanently archived',  tone:'honour', d:'M4 8h16v12H4zM2 4h20v4H2z'},
    {href:'/blog',     label:'Blog',         sub:'Stories and methodology notes',        tone:'plain',  d:'M4 5h16M4 10h16M4 15h10'},
    {href:'/status',   label:'Status',       sub:'Is everything working?',               tone:'plain',  d:'M3 12h4l3-7 4 14 3-7h4'}
  ]}
] %}
<div class="ag-head" data-ag-head>
  <header class="ag-head__bar">
    <a class="ag-logo" href="/" aria-label="{{ 'Africa GATES home'|trans }}">
      <img class="ag-logo__mark" src="{{ asset('/assets/img/logo-mark.png') }}" width="32" height="32" alt="">
      <span class="ag-logo__word" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ag-logo__africa">Africa</span><span class="ag-logo__gates">GATES</span></span>
    </a>

    <nav class="ag-head__nav" aria-label="{{ 'Primary'|trans }}">
      {% for m in _megas %}
        <button type="button" class="ag-head__top" id="ag-mega-{{ m.k }}-trigger"
                data-ag-mega-trigger="{{ m.k }}" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="ag-mega-{{ m.k }}">{{ m.label|trans }}<svg class="ag-head__chev" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.8 7.2 10 11 6.2 7.2 5 8.3l5 5 5-5z"></path></svg></button>
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>

    <span class="ag-head__gap"></span>

    <div class="ag-head__end">
      <div class="ag-tools-wrap">
        <div class="ag-tools" role="toolbar" aria-label="{{ 'Search, accessibility and language'|trans }}" data-ag-toolbar>
          <a class="ag-tools__b ag-tools__search" href="/discover" data-ag-search-open
             aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="{{ 'Search Africa GATES'|trans }}" title="{{ 'Search (/)'|trans }}">
            <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle><path d="m20 20-3.6-3.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg>
          </a>
          <span class="ag-tools__div" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <button type="button" class="ag-tools__b ag-tools__aa" data-ag-pop="aa" aria-haspopup="dialog"
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="ag-pop-aa" aria-label="{{ 'Display and reading'|trans }}"
                  title="{{ 'Display and reading'|trans }}">Aa</button>
          <span class="ag-tools__div" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {# The CODE on the pill, the language in full in the name: two letters fit a 40px
             pill and eight names do not, and nobody should need to know "ig" is Igbo. #}
          <button type="button" class="ag-tools__b ag-tools__lang" data-ag-pop="lang" aria-haspopup="menu"
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="ag-pop-lang"
                  aria-label="{{ 'Language: %name%'|trans({'%name%': lang_name()}) }}">
            <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.7 3.8 5.7 3.8 9s-1.3 6.3-3.8 9c-2.5-2.7-3.8-5.7-3.8-9S9.5 5.7 12 3Z"></path></svg>{{ lang()|upper }}
          </button>
        </div>

        {# Display & reading is the SHARED partial — the same one the Menu's sub-view
           uses — because two copies of seven switches is how the halves of a setting
           come to disagree. `uid` keeps its ids unique in a document holding both. #}
        <div class="ag-pop ag-pop--aa" id="ag-pop-aa" data-ag-pop-panel="aa" role="dialog"
             aria-label="{{ 'Display and reading'|trans }}" hidden>
          {% include 'partials/display-reading.twig' with { uid: 'aa' } %}
        </div>

        {# Links, so the middleware stores the choice on a plain navigation and the menu
           works with scripting off. Each name carries its own `lang`, so a screen reader
           says "Français" in French. #}
        <div class="ag-pop ag-pop--lang" id="ag-pop-lang" data-ag-pop-panel="lang" role="menu"
             aria-label="{{ 'Language'|trans }}" hidden>
          {% for l in languages() %}
            <a class="ag-pop__lang" role="menuitemradio" href="{{ lang_url(l.code) }}" hreflang="{{ l.code }}"
               aria-checked="{{ l.code == lang() ? 'true' : 'false' }}"><span lang="{{ l.code }}" dir="{{ l.dir }}">{{ l.name }}</span><span class="ag-pop__code" aria-hidden="true">{{ l.code|upper }}</span></a>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      {# REFERENCE §7.1 puts a cart icon with a count badge here "on shop routes, or
         whenever the cart isn't empty". There is no basket to read: the only one was a
         browser store written by the shop pages destroyed on 3 Oct 2026, and no server
         service holds one. A badge with nothing behind it would be a fake count, so
         there is none until Phase 7 builds the basket (docs/handoff/PHASE-2.md). #}
      {% if is_member %}
        <a class="ag-head__av" href="/account" aria-label="{{ 'Your account'|trans }}">{{ _ini }}</a>
      {% else %}
        <a class="ag-head__signin" href="/account/login">{{ 'Sign in'|trans }}</a>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>

  {% for m in _megas %}
    <div class="ag-mega" id="ag-mega-{{ m.k }}" data-ag-mega-panel="{{ m.k }}" role="menu"
         aria-labelledby="ag-mega-{{ m.k }}-trigger" hidden>
      <div class="ag-mega__in">
        {% for i in m.items %}
          <a class="ag-mega__item" role="menuitem" href="{{ i.href }}">
            <span class="ag-mega__tile ag-tone--{{ i.tone }}" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="{{ i.d }}"></path></svg></span>
            <span class="ag-mega__txt"><span class="ag-mega__t">{{ i.label|trans }}</span><span class="ag-mega__s">{{ i.sub|trans }}</span></span>
          </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {# The transparent scrim below an open panel: a click anywhere off it closes it. #}
  <div class="ag-mega-scrim" data-ag-mega-scrim hidden></div>
</div>
